# AlgoRico Frontend UI, Forms, And Quality

- Build screens with shadcn/ui and existing primitives from `src/components/ui`, `src/components/layout`, and `src/components/feedback` before adding new primitives.
- Use Tailwind classes through existing `cn` helpers and keep responsive states explicit.
- User-facing copy is Spanish; keep labels, toasts, loading, empty, and error states consistent.
- Validate forms with Zod schemas and `react-hook-form`; show field errors through shared form primitives.
- Use compound components only where related subparts share state or structure, such as `Dialog`, `DialogTrigger`, and `DialogContent`.
- Every data-driven route should handle loading, empty, error, and forbidden states where applicable.
- Keep interactive controls accessible with labels, button `type`, keyboard-friendly behavior, and semantic roles when needed.
- This app is mobile first.
- Before finishing substantive frontend changes, run available checks from this package: `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm run test`, and `npm run build` when practical.
